    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nContemporary bungalow residence set on 2.5 acres approx. commanding a scenic sunny south facing aspect on the Sheeps Head peninsula. This impressive residence enjoys a spectacular rural coastal setting adjacent to Glanlough Lake and is ideally located between Bantry Bay and Dunmanus Bay in West Cork. Bantry, Durrus, Ahakista and Kilcrohane are all convenient to this home.\n\nThe property is extensively upgraded and modernised in recent years, creating a bright, spacious and contemporary home while retaining the peace and character of its rural surroundings. The elevated position ensures the views are enjoyed throughout the property while a glass-fronted balcony to the front provides the perfect vantage point from which to sit back and take in the tranquil surroundings.\n\nThe accommodation begins with an entrance hall leading into a generous open-plan living, kitchen and dining area. Bi-fold doors open onto the front balcony and patio doors lead to the rear, creating an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces. The extensive glazing allows the spectacular surroundings to become an integral part of the home while two new skylights, installed as part \nof the recent renovation, further enhance the natural light.\n\nThere is a large utility room with external access, a family bathroom and three well-proportioned bedrooms, two of which are ensuite. The principal bedroom is particularly impressive with bi-fold doors opening directly onto the balcony, creating a wonderful private space from which to enjoy the beautiful views and peaceful surroundings.\n\nThe property occupies a substantial 2.5-acre site, offering considerable privacy, space and potential in an exceptionally scenic location. The surrounding grounds provide ample opportunity for outdoor enjoyment while the elevated position creates an enviable sense of space and connection with the landscape. To the rear, magnificent views stretch over Bantry Bay, where the changing light, surrounding countryside, and distant coastline create a stunning outlook year-round.\n\nLocated on the renowned Sheep's Head Peninsula, this is a wonderfully peaceful part of West Cork, celebrated for its rugged coastline, spectacular scenery and unspoilt natural beauty. Yet the property remains within convenient reach of the amenities and services of the surrounding villages of Ahakista (5km approx.), Durrus (9km approx.) and the bustling market town of Bantry (13km approx.). \n\nDisclaimer\nWhilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct, but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
      },
